.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LIBTRACECMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tracecmp_open
.Nd explicitly authorized DTrace descriptor delegation
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libtracecmp
.Pq Fl ltracecmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In tracecmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn tracecmp_open "int *dtracefd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn tracecmp_open
connects to the global
.Dq org.5bsd.trace
service through
.Xr libservice 3 ,
negotiates version 1.0.0, and requests one DTrace consumer descriptor.
Applications do not supply a component or provider name.
.Pp
The base provider currently advertises no raw-descriptor feature and rejects
the open operation with
.Er EACCES .
Any future provider that implements this interface deliberately exposes raw
DTrace authority and is suitable only under an explicit administrator policy.
Such a descriptor must have a complete DTrace ioctl allowlist, be
non-transferable, and be closed on exec.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr tracecmp 8
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Capsicum rights and ioctl lists cannot express D language probe, predicate,
or action policy.
A future broker-owned session API should be preferred for untrusted tracing
programs.
